  "summary": {
    "intent": "Set up and run a design-sync workflow to migrate the CipherBox web app's ~83 React components into a Claude design system project, generating previews, screenshots, and grading each component's render fidelity.",
    "outcome": "Successfully bundled the app via a converter, wired up providers/polyfills/store seeding so components render correctly, fanned out six parallel sub-agents that authored and graded previews for all 68 remaining components (nearly all 'good'), applied config overrides, and pushed batches to the CipherBox Design System project; two components (StagingBanner, MigrationProgress) were left on the floor card due to unfixable config-level blockers.",
    "learnings": {
      "repo": [
        "The converter's `import.meta.env` define (`IIFE_IMPORT_META_DEFINE` in `.ds-sync/lib/common.mjs`) only provides MODE, DEV, PROD, SSR, BASE_URL — any component gating on a custom env var like VITE_ENVIRONMENT always renders null in previews",
        "The preview frame (`.design-sync/DsFrame.tsx`) never calls `setApiClientConfig` from `@cipherbox/api-client`, so any component making live API calls (e.g. MigrationProgress via migrationApi.getStatus()) throws and renders null",
        "MatrixBackground uses `position: fixed; z-index: -1` and needs a preview wrapper with `position: relative; z-index: 1` to create a stacking context so it's visible in the card",
        "NotificationToast is `position: fixed` bottom-right; wrapping with `transform: translateZ(0)` contains the stack inside the card",
        "SharedListRow/SharedFolderRow require an ancestor with class `shared-browser` because `.file-list-row` grid rules in shared-browser.css are scoped under it",
        "SharedFolderRow's `isSelected` prop has no corresponding `.file-list-row--selected` style — an app-level styling gap, not a preview issue",
        "SharedFileBrowser and InviteLinkTab load data via hooks (useSharedNavigation) that call the API on mount and write to component state, unreachable via store seeding — needs an API stub seam",
        "FileBrowser reads root from `useFolderStore.folders.root`, not `useVaultStore`; seeded nodes need `folderKey: null` and `sequenceNumber: BigInt(12)`",
        "BinBrowser's `isLoading`/`error` are local `useBin` state and cannot be seeded via stores",
        "BinBrowser, BinEmptyState, BinListItem, SyncIndicator are missing from `file-browser/index.ts` barrel yet still exported by the bundle — barrel is not the real export contract",
        "ContextMenu portals to document.body with fixed positioning; since each story captures on its own page, positioning it at x=24,y=24 keeps it inside the card",
        "package-capture.mjs loads one story per page (`?story=<CellName>`), so module-top store seeds don't leak between components, but store-reading components can sweep multiple states within one cell via `useMemo(() => useXStore.setState({...}), [deps])`",
        "StorageTab must not see a seeded `vaultKeypair` or it derives a BYO IPNS keypair and hangs resolving an IPNS record; ConnectionTest and StorageTab should seed useAuthStore with teeKeys only",
        "Story cells have fixed slot heights and are laid out alphabetically by export name; taller content gets clipped, especially if placed last",
        "Real PerFileUpload statuses are `encrypting`, `uploading`, `complete`, `error` — differs from what was assumed in the sub-agent brief"
      ],
      "code": [
        {
          "path": ".design-sync/DsFrame.tsx",
          "finding": "Preview frame lacks setApiClientConfig call for @cipherbox/api-client, causing all live API calls in previewed components to throw"
        }
      ],
      "workflow": [
        "Fanning out parallel sub-agents with a shared brief works well for authoring/grading previews across independent component batches, but each agent must record config-level blockers separately since fixes belong in shared files (DsFrame.tsx) applied once by the orchestrator after all agents report",
        "After parallel agents finish, verify they stayed within their assigned file scope before folding in their learnings and overrides",
        "Running captures in parallel across agents can cause transient timeouts (`page.goto: Timeout 20000ms exceeded`); simply re-running only the failed components resolves it",
        "Cross-check every named class, token, and export in a written conventions/header doc against the actual build output before considering it final"
      ]
    },
    "friction": [
      "import.meta.env define in the converter blocks any component gating on custom env vars (StagingBanner, part of AppShell) with no preview-level workaround",
      "Preview frame missing API client config blocks any component making live API calls (MigrationProgress, partially StorageTab)",
      "Fixed-position/portaled components (MatrixBackground, NotificationToast, ContextMenu, SearchPalette) required per-component preview wrapper hacks to render correctly inside story cards",
      "Sub-agent's initial brief had an incorrect assumption about UploadListItem's status prop values, requiring correction during preview authoring",
      "Parallel screenshot captures across agents caused transient page.goto timeouts for some components",
      "Fixed slot heights in story cells clip taller content (e.g. FileDetails with multiple version entries), requiring cardMode/viewport overrides"
    ],
    "open_items": [
      "StagingBanner and the staging branch of AppShell remain unrenderable in previews until the converter's import.meta.env define is extended or overridden",
      "MigrationProgress remains on the floor card until DsFrame.tsx calls setApiClientConfig; the migration block inside StorageTab is similarly hidden",
      "SharedFileBrowser and InviteLinkTab's loaded-list states need an API stub seam since store seeding can't reach their internal hook state",
      "SharedFolderRow's missing `.file-list-row--selected` style is an app-level gap worth fixing outside the design-sync effort",
      "FileDetails with a full (unclipped) version list may need the suggested override `{\"cardMode\":\"single\",\"viewport\":\"760x900\"}` if the complete list is desired in the design system"
    ]
  },
